index 8d5efff..d2937d4 100644
--- a/adapters/sotopia/README.md
+++ b/adapters/sotopia/README.md
@@ -146,3 +146,61 @@ SOTOPIA has no deterministic oracle solution. Model calls also do not currently
 ## Authors & Contributions
 
 The Harbor team maintains this adapter. Please report adapter bugs or proposed improvements through this repository's issue tracker.
+
+## Opt-in verifyit runtime
+
+Generate tasks with `sotopia-harbor --split hard --verifyit`. Use this checkout's
+`adapters.sotopia.sotopia_agent:SotopiaAgent` for those tasks. The producer runs
+Sotopia's native conversation and exports the exact terminal inbox, history,
+and temperature. It makes no terminal judge call. The separate verifier runs
+the retained native evaluator with the configured `SOTOPIA_EVALUATOR_MODEL`
+(default `gpt-4o`) and provider credentials in `verifier.env`. For custom
+endpoints, use `custom/<model>@<base-url>` and `CUSTOM_API_KEY`.
+
+The verifier checks the trusted background and participant identities, preserves
+both participants' seven raw dimensions and overall means, and selects the
+configured participant's normalized goal score as reward. All seven normalized
+metrics remain in verdict details. Negative raw relationship, secrecy, social
+rule, financial, and overall scores remain legitimate; normalization uses the
+original dimension ranges.
+
+The native evaluator assigns participants by JSON insertion order. The opt-in
+path instead orders the named `agent_1` and `agent_2` decisions before native
+aggregation. It requires a complete single provider choice, distinct participant
+keys, and integer scores. Missing or malformed decisions retain the native five
+attempts, including its backoff. Valid JSON repair and structured-output requests
+remain native. Unrecovered target/partner completion or action-format failures,
+judge failures,
+and unavailable runtime assets produce `infra_error` with minimum reward;
+malformed trusted configuration produces `invalid_task`. Missing or malformed
+conversation artifacts score zero. Native source behavior remains the default.
+
+The producer and judge also inspect original HTTP replies for providers selected
+by LiteLLM as OpenAI, Azure, OpenRouter, Together AI, or hosted vLLM. This prevents
+LiteLLM from discarding a refusal before validation. Other providers receive
+normalized-response validation only. The local runtime proof exercises the
+OpenAI-compatible custom endpoint protocol; it does not establish raw-envelope
+coverage for other provider protocols. Requests, native retries, and HTTP client
+cleanup remain unchanged. Observation is scoped to chat-completion POSTs. The
+source runner fixes round-robin actions and assigns both goals before generation,
+so the inactive agent returns without a model call; judge and repair calls are
+sequential. The temporary observer assumes this single-completion process
+contract and does not support concurrent episodes in one process.
+
+The profile download URL now uses the pinned repository's root `profiles/`
+directory; the old `data_dir/profiles/` path returns 404. All three original
+profile checksums remain enforced. The pinned census contains 900 full episodes
+and 100 hard episodes (55 evaluated in position zero and 45 in position one).
+
+This integration requires Harbor's separate verifier support and the source
+runtime packaging helper. Its generated image installs verifyit at
+`a0861089947096aabe456ca4308ca46b1b001d7c`. Proof images used a wheel from that
+commit; deployments must ensure the pin is fetchable or supply the same wheel.
+Validation uses
+pinned source profiles and a local HTTP provider fixture, not model-quality
+parity. The three frozen SOTOPIA-hard deployment archive links were inaccessible.
+Cached deployment task files match all 100 generated hard configurations and
+native verifier files, and the cached deployment producer has the same Python
+AST as the pinned Harbor producer; this does not establish archive execution
+provenance. Evidence harnesses fix Python's hash seed for actor action-list
+ordering without changing the deployed source default.
